      <activity id="58708038-62b6-5a5a-b9c5-c8f4030917c3" activityNameId="68475382-a5a2-5cd4-b55b-b5af8e70e3ac" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Irrigating</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Irrigating
Inventory refers to the irrigation of 1 m3 fresh water. ;
UUID: f6ea3291-55fe-3738-af23-943b7be1a4e3
The inventory includes the processes of water pumping (from a depth of 48m), machine infrastructure and a shed for machine sheltering. The water used is also included (as ground water).
Location: Refers to average irrigation in the USA
Technology: conventional production typical for the country
Time period: undefined
Production volume: US average use of irrigated water is about 10700 Mio m3 per year.  
Sampling: Data come from varoius U.S database. Data were compiled from statistics and expert knowledge 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f6ea3291-55fe-3738-af23-943b7be1a4e3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
